name: Marathon
chapter: 01
when: 490 BC
where: the plain of Marathon, Attica
who: Miltiades' Athenians vs Datis and Artaphernes
road: dust
brief: A plain a mile wide with mountains behind it, a marsh at one end and the bay at the other. The Athenians thinned their centre, ran the last two hundred yards, and were home before the Persian fleet could sail round.
